WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.268 --> 00:00:04.299
- [Narrator] For a few weeks
between the wet and dry seasons,

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:07.087
this seemingly ordinary
looking river bursts

00:00:07.087 --> 00:00:09.324
to life with color.

00:00:09.324 --> 00:00:10.702
(water splashing)

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:13.369
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.854 --> 00:00:20.706
Caño Cristales is located
in Meta, Colombia.

00:00:20.706 --> 00:00:22.461
When the conditions are just right,

00:00:22.461 --> 00:00:24.581
an endemic aquatic plant species

00:00:24.581 --> 00:00:26.873
that lives in the riverbed blooms,

00:00:26.873 --> 00:00:29.453
creating a brilliant show of red color,

00:00:29.453 --> 00:00:33.953
often with hints of yellow,
orange, green, and blue.

00:00:33.953 --> 00:00:36.473
Because of this, locals refer to the river

00:00:36.473 --> 00:00:40.640
as the liquid rainbow, or
the River of Five Colors.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:45.153
Before 2009, the Caño
Cristales was closed off

00:00:45.153 --> 00:00:47.265
to the public due to guerrilla activity

00:00:47.265 --> 00:00:49.754
in the surrounding region.

00:00:49.754 --> 00:00:53.128
Today, the river can be reached
by horseback or by foot,

00:00:53.128 --> 00:00:56.788
and is accessible under the
guidance of local tour guides.

00:00:56.788 --> 00:00:59.310
Although this phenomenon only
happens for a short period

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.054
of time each year, this living rainbow

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:03.962
leaves a lasting impression.

00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:06.629
(upbeat music)

